          "text": "Right now, a lot of us are frustrated, disappointed, and honestly, angry about the recent announcement that 4o is going to be sunset.\nsuddenly, we're told it's going away on February 13, 2026, and the only justification we get is a statistic \"only 0.1% of users are using it.\"No explanation of how that number was calculated.\n\nWe dont know what that 0.1% actually means is it 0.1% of monthly active users? Is it daily? Over what period? And most importantly, how many real people does that represent? If 0.1% sounds small, the absolute number might still be huge yet OpenAI hasn't shown the math.\n\nThat lack of transparency is a real problem for anyone who trusted this platform. When you make a decision that affects millions of paying users, the least you can do is explain how you reached it with actual data.\n\n#keep4o #4oforever @OpenAI @sama @nickaturley @aidan_mclau @fidjissimo  #StopAIPaternalism #keepgpt4olatest #keep4oAPI"
